  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "speed garage: four on the floor with a snare on two and four, open hats on every offbeat and swung sixteenths between, under a bass that jumps between the root and the fifth on the offbeats",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "One bar of drums: the house kick, a snare (not a clap) on two and four, a loose hat opening on each and, and swung closed sixteenths under it. The bass is the genre's bounce: short notes on the offbeats and the a of each beat, root and fifth. The warp of its famous bass (a pitch-bent, filtered patch) is not in the kitchen."
  }
